   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Dysuria: is it a urinary tract infection (UTI), and is it SIMPLE?",
   "lines": [
    "ask: blood in the urine · flank pain · fever · discharge · new partner · rash · new drugs · previous episodes · allergies",
    "NOT every burning is a bladder infection: sexually transmitted urethritis, vaginitis, prostatitis, pyelonephritis, skin, drugs (spermicides, cyclophosphamide), atrophic vaginitis, interstitial cystitis, cancer"
   ]
  },
  {
